": 79, "color": "B", "move": "pass", "lead_before": 8.07, "lead_after": 8.0, "points_lost": 0.07, "best": "G8"}], "review": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "title": "A 9.9-Point Lead Handed Back, Then Four Passes", "summary": "Black, the 10k, won by 8 points (B+8) after two passes. The two sides lost almost the same per move (Opus 5.5 2.2, the 10k 2.4), and the lead changed hands several times. White had its best moment at move 27 and gave it straight back at move 28. The late passes at 58 to 64 each cost about 7.5 points and left Black with the margin that held to the end.", "moments": [{"turn": 8, "text": "White's D4 moved the lead from +0.4 to +5.1 for Black and lost 4.7 points. The engine preferred E3. It was the first big swing against Opus 5.5, and it came right after the stones started touching in the centre."}, {"turn": 27, "text": "The 10k's H8 lost 7.8 points and took Black's lead from -2.1 to -9.9. This was White's best moment of the game, with a wall of stones across rows 3 to 7 and Black's G-column stones standing apart from it."}, {"turn": 28, "text": "Opus 5.5 answered with C4, which lost 9.9 points, the worst move of the game, and the lead went from -9.9 back to +0.0. The engine wanted G2. Nearly the whole advantage from the 10k's mistake went in one move."}, {"turn": 34, "text": "D8 lost 7.3 points and moved the lead from -2.0 to +5.3 for Black. The engine's choice was E1. It came right after the 10k's own 5.9-point slip at move 33, so the lead had just swung the other way."}, {"turn": 58, "text": "Opus 5.5 passed with Black at +8.1, and the lead went to +15.6, a loss of 7.5 points. The engine's choice was C2. White passed again at 60, 62 and 64 with the same result, and by move 64 the White stones on the H column were gone, with 5 captured by Black. These passes mattered more than any single stone in the middle game."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "Every command ran libs.py, which reads a pasted board and flood-fills each group to print its stones, liberties and a DANGER flag for 2 or fewer liberties; it never tries moves, scores points, or looks ahead, so it only inspected the current position.", "stop": false}}